  "description": "YUSSUB crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H115 Er5 O25,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1C (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1B (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.522-4.981 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.61-156.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C164H131Er5O25.",
